{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>Speak to the children of Israel.</b> He equalized all of them to be dispatched with this utterance — for they were equal in agreement and accepted upon themselves the decree of the Omnipresent out of love." "<b>This is the living creature.</b> The language of חַיִּים, life — because Israel are joined to the Omnipresent and worthy to live; therefore He separated them from impurity and decreed commandments upon them, and the nations He forbade nothing. A parable of a physician who entered to examine the sick one, etc. — as is found in Midrash Rabbi Tanchuma." "<b>This is the living creature.</b> This teaches that Moses would hold the living creature and show it to Israel: ״This you may eat and this you may not eat״ (Hullin 42a); ״These you may eat״ etc. (verse 9) — also with the water-creatures he held every single species and showed them, and likewise with the fowl: ״And these you shall detest among the fowl״ (verse 13), and likewise with the creeping things: ״And this is impure to you״ (verse 29)." "<b>This is the living creature … of all the animals.</b> This teaches that the domesticated animal is included in the living creature (Sifra; Hullin 70a)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:05:47.917219204Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}